+# Aurora atmosphere.2 — scaled post passes and cloud history
+
+Local opt-in API `0.1-aurora-atmosphere.2`, extending atmosphere.1. The shared
+432-byte frame and existing material/sky/shadow contracts are unchanged. Earlier
+APIs keep the original full-resolution ping-pong renderer and cannot request
+these new manifest keys. This is a fork API, not an upstream release.
+
+Each `[[post]]` may set `resolution_divisor = 1`, `2`, or `4` (default 1).
+Intermediate dimensions are `ceil(world_dimension / divisor)`, at least 1 pixel.
+`PostInput.pixel` is in the current pass target, `uv` remains normalized and
+`frame.resolution` remains the world size. `previous` is the preceding pass at
+its own dimensions. The final pass must be full resolution and cannot retain
+history; sky and material cannot set these keys.
+
+One non-final pass may set `history = true`. Its half-float output is copied to a
+persistent texture immediately after that pass, before the ping-pong slot can be
+reused. A separate R32Float image stores the scene depth at the retained target's
+resolution after all post consumers. This snapshot is an extra small render pass,
+not a copy of the final colour or the hand/HUD. All render targets are bounded by
+the existing pass limit and the three supported resolutions.
+
+The retained pass can read group 3 resources:
+
+- binding 6: `history_color: texture_2d<f32>`, the same pass's preceding result;
+- binding 7: `history_depth: texture_2d<f32>`, nearest scene depth from that frame;
+- binding 8: `post_history`, a 96-byte uniform: previous camera-relative
+  view-projection matrix, `camera_delta.xyz` (current camera minus previous),
+  `camera_delta.w` (history valid), and `clock.xy` (previous/current wrapped seconds).
+
+Only the pass marked `history=true` has defined historical contents. Other post
+passes must not consume these bindings. A pack is responsible for reprojection,
+visibility rejection, neighbourhood clamping and choosing a blend weight. Depth
+is the same reversed opaque-world depth as atmosphere.1, not transparent geometry.
+
+New pack instances, reloads, resized/replaced world targets, nonconsecutive frames,
+dimension/water-medium changes, camera translations of 8+ blocks, large direction
+or projection changes, time jumps, weather jumps and frame gaps of 250+ ms invalidate
+history. The first frame seeds it. Small camera motion uses the preceding exact
+projection (including camera effects/TAA jitter). Lunar phase and existing water
+uniform offsets stay unchanged. History is kept in GPU memory, never in world saves.
+
+Aurora's prototype retains only cloud radiance/transmittance, with 16 jittered
+integration steps. It accumulates sky pixels, rejects previous foreground depth,
+uses a representative point at cloud height 184 (an approximation), compensates
+procedural cloud drift and clamps old colour/opacity to a current 3×3 neighbourhood.
+Motion above 16 half-resolution pixels rejects accumulation; intermediate motion
+reduces its weight. Clouds drawn in front of opaque depth use the current frame
+only. This is not a general TAA implementation or a guarantee against all ghosting.
+
+Tests cover manifest boundaries and legacy rejection, translation to all three
+backends, clock wrapping/camera cuts, and a required GPU test of odd-sized scaled
+passes, floating-point history, previous depth, reset on cut/resize/pack reload.
+The shadow GPU suite also exercises atmosphere.2 with Low and High receivers.
+Run both suites with `AURORA_REQUIRE_GPU=1`; missing hardware must fail preflight.
